Q ¶ __Then likewise he shall say,__
P O Lord, open thou our lips:
P __Answ.__ And our mouth shall shew forth thy
  praise.
P __Priest.__ O God, make speed to save us.
P __Answ.__ O Lord, make haste to help us.
Q ¶ __Here all standing up, the Priest shall say,__
P Glory be to the Father, and to the Son: and
  to the holy Ghost;
P __Answ.__ As it was in the beginning, is now,
  and ever shall be: world without end. __Amen.__
P __Priest.__ Praise ye the Lord.
P __Answ.__ The Lord’s Name be praised.
R ¶ __Then shall be said or sung this Psalm following: except on__ Easter-
  day, __upon which another Anthem is appointed: and on the Nine-__
  __teenth day of every Month it is not to be read here, but in the or-__
  __dinary course of the Psalms.__
T __Venite, exultemus Domino.__ Psal. xcv.
I O Come, let us sing unto the Lord: let us
  heartily rejoice in the strength of our sal-
  vation.
P Let us come before his presence with thanks-
  giving: and shew ourselves glad in him with
  psalms.
P For the Lord is a great God: and a great
  King above all gods.
P In his hand are all the corners of the earth:
